{
  "primitive": "htcrypt",
  "source": "HeavyThing htcrypt.inc self-consistency (round-trip identity) vectors. htcrypt is a custom 16-byte block cipher (64-deep AES-256 cascade); NOT a published standard, so the authoritative property is decrypt(encrypt(p))==p (AAP \u00a70.4.2). The harness performs the full round trip (or hide/show wrap+unwrap then round trip) and emits the recovered plaintext, so expected_hex == plaintext_hex for every positive case. negative_wrong_key decrypts under a different secret and asserts the result differs from the plaintext (expect_mismatch).",
  "vectors": [
